Modifications to the manifest data as vendored here:

  - Alias entries carrying the upstream project's own "herdr:" namespace prefix
    were removed from the pi, opencode and kilo manifests. Those aliases name
    the upstream project's internal identifiers and mean nothing outside it.

  - One comment in the grok manifest named the upstream project as the reader of
    an OSC 9;4 payload; it now says "the engine", which is what it describes.

Everything else in the vendored files - identifiers, versions, timestamps, rule
bodies and comments - is carried verbatim, so that a copy held here can be
compared byte for byte against the upstream release it came from.

No source code from the herdr project is used. The herdr name appears in this
crate only in this file and in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.
